{%- comment -%}
  Shown on posts with `draft: true` — reuses .post-aside (the {% aside %} shortcode's callout
  styling, see .eleventy.js) rather than a parallel box style. `draft` is purely a visual notice
  here: it doesn't exclude the post from the blog listing, RSS feed, or sitemap.
{%- endcomment -%}
<aside role="note" class="post-aside draft-note">
  <p class="draft-note__heading">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path>
    </svg>
    Work in Progress
  </p>
  <p class="draft-note__body">
    The content you are about to read is still a work in progress. Because of the topic's nuances
    and my quest for perfection, I'm still fine-tuning the details. But I couldn't wait to share
    what I have so far with you! Got some brilliant ideas to add or spot something that needs
    fixing? I'd love to hear from you! Your insights are incredibly valuable and can help make this
    post even better. Drop me a line at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> with
    your thoughts, suggestions, or any corrections. Thanks!
  </p>
</aside>
